  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1048 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nThe long term forecast will be largely dominated by a strong upper\nridge that will bring a relatively dry but hot airmass to the area.\nHighs on Sunday will climb to the low 90s while large scale\nsubsidence and afternoon mixing help keep heat indices near or below\nthe 100 degree mark. As the upper ridge builds in and becomes better\namplified next week, H85 temps will climb to the 20-25C range,\ntranslating to sfc temps in the mid to upper 90s. The good news that\nmay suppress a larger heat wave threat will be that the dewpoint\ntemps are slightly lower than what we have seen in recent events. \nEven still, afternoon heat indices will rise to the 100-107 degree \nrange next week and any trends that favor a slightly more moist \nenvironment would work to increase the risk for dangerous heat. \nSummer is not over yet, so remember to practice and plan for \ndangerous temps and very hot outdoor working conditions. The limited\nmoisture and lack of more synoptic support for thunderstorms will\nkeep PoPs capped below 20% through the long term period.",
